, or about C$3.56B annualised.\n- **Industry:** Transformer shipments fell 4% year on year in Q2 2026, the first decline in three years. Growth had already slowed from +3.1% in 2025Q4 to +1.8% in 2026Q1.\n- **Voltaris shipments:** They fell 9% in Q2, the steepest among large makers.\n- **Market share:** Voltaris's share of shipments fell from 31% to 27%. Tarnwell and imports gained.\n- **Orders lead shipments:** Shipments trail orders by about two quarters. Voltaris's H1 2026 orders were up 11% (from n2's document). That may support some shipment recovery in late 2026 and 2027, but I haven't analysed it.\n\n**Implied 2027 revenue**\n- If the industry is flat to slightly up (0–3%) and Voltaris holds a 27% share, revenue is about C$3.5–3.7B.\n- If the share loss continues, revenue falls toward C$3.3–3.5B.\n- Reaching C$4.2B needs an industry rebound of roughly 5–8% combined with a share recovery to about 30–31%. Neither is visible in the data.\n- The 11% order growth is the main upside risk, and I haven't tested it against shipments or revenue.\n\n**Caveats:** I don't have the industry's full-year shipment level or the revenue mix of transformers versus other products. I assumed revenue tracks transformer shipments, and the scenarios above are my own rough scaling, not model output.","ttft_ms":2383,"type":"result","duration_ms":22343,"uuid":"0eb2f41b-c8b9-4483-9e02-f6bb1cea5146","ttft_stream_ms":1454,"time_to_request_ms":415,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":13,"system_prompt":8,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":17,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":26,"tool_pool_refresh":10,"init_message":72,"init_frame_send":26,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":19,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":38,"request_announcements":93,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":2,"tool_schema_build":6,"message_normalization":11,"client_creation":44,"request_build":17},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_req